  "worked_solution": "We need to solve the following system consisting of the equations of the curves:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y={x}^{2}-2 \\\\ y=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the equations equal to one another and solving, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2 & =x \\\\ {x}^{2}-x-2 & =0 \\\\ (x+1)(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-1,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinates of the intersection points are ${x}_{1}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-1+2=1.\n$$",
